# Target C — C72 radial cut-transport frontier

**LEVEL I STATUS: STILL OPEN.**

Full proof: [target_c_radial_cut_transport_2026-08-31.md](../../reports/target_c_radial_cut_transport_2026-08-31.md).

C71 reduces the `D epsilon -> 0` phase to either a multi-port return component at the mechanical star center `z`, or one single physical contact port carrying essentially all star load. C72 quantifies the stress transport after that port.

For `r_i=|p_i-z|`, define

`Q_z=sum_C alpha_ij[1-(r_i-r_j)^2]`

and

`T_z=sum_C alpha_ij |r_i-r_j|`.

Then

`Q_z/2 <= D^2-T_z <= Q_z`.

Since C68 gives `Q_z<=D^2(1-S_z)`,

`T_z>=D^2 S_z`.

At the C66 center,

`T_z>=D^2-(2pi/kappa_0)D^3 epsilon`.

The exact Euclidean radial coarea identity is

`T_z=integral_0^D A_z(t) dt`,

where `A_z(t)` is total contact stress crossing `{r<t}`.

There is also a contact-graph cut law. Put `ell(v)=d_C(z,v)` and `L=ceil(D)`. Every diameter partner of `z` has `ell>=L`. For every `0<=j<L`, summed KKT equilibrium on `U_j={ell<=j}` gives

`A_j>=|g_z|-2D(1-S_z)`.

The corresponding cut edge sets are disjoint in stress measure, so

`A_up>=L[|g_z|-2D(1-S_z)]_+`.

C14 yields

`|g_z|>=(sqrt(3)/2)D S_z`,

hence in the near-zero phase

`liminf A_up/D^2>=sqrt(3)/2`.

Together C68, C71, and C72 force the single-port branch into an aggregate normal form:

- one `Omega(D)` port edge;
- depth at least `ceil(D)` before a star diameter leaf;
- every pre-leaf graph cut transmits `Omega(D)` stress;
- at least `sqrt(3)/2-o(1)` of all alpha mass lies on graph-outward contacts; and
- the alpha-weighted Euclidean radial progress is `D^2-o(D^2)`.

C67 simultaneously forces a quadratic-area force hull. The remaining escape is therefore two-dimensional geometry carried by asymptotically negligible transverse stress.

## Next target

Do not try to squeeze more from one fixed alpha measure. The next useful input must charge low-stress transverse structure independently: KKT-certificate variation, reciprocal-dual width/area, contact-minimal source capacity, or quantitative closure of C71-A's return/separator branch.